{"title":"Introduction to Entrepreneurship: Is This for Me, and Where Do I Start?","startsAt":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-05T20:00:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"Most people don't hesitate because their idea is bad. They hesitate because they think entrepreneurship is intimidating. This opening session challenges this assumption by using real Canadian statistics and introducing the Business Model Canvas, both of which can help you capture how a business creates value, reaches customers, and generates capital. By the end of this session, you will be given a chance to start filling in your own Business Model Canvas and a chance to network with other participants.\n\nThe program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\n\nPresented by Ryan Knight, TPL's 2026 [Entrepreneur in Residence](https://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/featured/entrepreneur-in-residence/) (EIR) at Toronto Reference Library.\n\n**Registration via TPL website:** [https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31)\n**Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.**\n\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: [tpl.ca/accessibility-events](https://tpl.ca/accessibility/accessibility-supports/programs-and-events/?_gl=1*v83hy7*_ga*NDk5MDg2NTE1LjE3NjYwMDgxODQ.*_ga_G99DMMNG39*czE3NjkxMDY3NDMkbzE0JGcxJHQxNzY5MTA2ODM0JGozOCRsMCRoMA..).","venue":{"name":"Toronto Public Library - Toronto Reference Library","address":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.671807,"lng":-79.386816,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/b/6/3/highres_536307491.jpeg"}